rting, serves `warn`) and `readme` (supporting, serves `warn`) all hold up.\n\n### 3. Removal candidates\n\nNone. Every group is needed for the task.\n\n### 4. Simplifications\n\nMinor: `floored` is built with a second `impactRank` check that duplicates the `signal` test. Not worth changing on its own.\n\n### 5. Missing risks\n\n- **Noise pushing filler ratings (read):** the warning fires on every non-mechanical group without `impact`, including docs-only and test-only groups such as `readme` and `test` in this very change. The skill's guidance is consistent with that, but authors may respond by writing `impact: \"local\"` on everything to silence the warning, which would make the field meaningless. Consider making the warning exclude groups whose hunks are all tests or docs, or at least watch for this pattern.\n- **Hidden when other errors exist (read):** `ratingProblems` runs only if `errors` is empty (`add.ts:55`), so the unrated warning is suppressed whenever another error is present. That is probably fine, but it is not documented.\n\n### Test run (verified in part)\n\n| File | Result |\n|---|---|\n| ary | 10 pass |\n| browser | 1 pass |\n| carry | 22 pass |\n| decisions | 11 pass |\n| impactwarn | 7 pass |\n| tmp | 4 pass |\n| attention | 25 pass, cut off at 45 s |\n| reviews | 7 pass, cut off at 45 s |\n| untrusted | 12 pass, cut off at 45 s |\n| gloss | 0 reported, cut off at 45 s |\n| signals | 0 reported, cut off at 45 s |\n\nNo test failed. The cut-off files are **unverified**, not failing. A full `npm test` did not finish within about 2.5 minutes. I did not check whether this slowness predates the change.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES\n\nAutonomous loop stopped. The review of the impact-warning change was already delivered in full, and nothing in this clone needs follow-up. No PR or CI is involved, and I made no changes. The one open item is the unverified test files, which I did not re-run because the remaining run would only repeat the earlier timeouts.","verdict